{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791578681,"nonce":"U2PwCEgnShQhOZEddG5ZY45V1ds=","title":"M3: Dedupe job groups by resolved application URL","message":"The same opening often arrives from several sources (national NLx, a state NLx site, USAJOBS, email alerts) with different text but the same application target. Add a dedupe pass keyed on the normalized application URL: job.apply_url at listing time and apply_link.final_url after resolution. Normalize: lowercase scheme and host, drop fragments except ATS-required ones, strip tracking params (utm_*, src, source, ref, gh_src, iis, iisn), canonical ATS form from ats_rules. Groups sharing a normalized URL merge (non-destructive, keeps all job rows, canonical prefers full description). Needs a job_group.method value apply_url, which means a migration that rebuilds job_group to extend its CHECK constraint. Re-run merge after apply-link resolution. Requested by the user.","files":null}]}